  "risk_conclusions": [
    "FMA prioritizes NaNs in multiplicand, multiplier, then addend order; it quiets the chosen signaling NaN. With alpha=1 and the emitted operand mapping unchanged, other wins over self when both are NaNs.",
    "Separate scalar ADD can propagate its first encoded NaN source. Source-level expression order does not alone prove encoded operand order or whether the compiler contracts into FMA.",
    "Therefore scalar and vector paths can differ for two NaNs. The fixed-wheel observation, or its actual machine code, must settle the result; these sources do not establish which path any particular layout takes.",
    "For opposite infinities without NaN inputs, masked x86 ADD/FMA invalid results use binary32 QNaNIndefinite 0xffc00000. This differs from a positive canonical 0x7fc00000 fallback.",
    "Only cmd95 is under review. This does not qualify general NaN propagation, floating exception flags, or the whole numerical runtime."
  ],
